// Keys (RSAPublicKey, DER) and signatures of "hello velt" (or of the message named with them)
// made with OpenSSL 3.0.13 (`openssl genpkey -algorithm RSA`, `openssl dgst -sign`, PSS with
// `rsa_pss_saltlen:digest` unless named otherwise), signatures of chosen encoded messages
// computed with the private key, and keys derived from the 2048-bit one by re-encoding its
// numbers. A name says the modulus's bits and, after "E", the bits of a public exponent that is
// not 65537 (E3 and E37 are those exponents). The 2049-bit key is two primes from
// `openssl prime -generate`: `genpkey` makes 2048 bits when asked for 2049.

